    "homeType": "MULTI_FAMILY",
    "description": "Built in 1904, this distinguished Edwardian 5-unit property is a tremendous opportunity. Nestled at the bottom of the first block of Fair Oaks at 22nd Street, this property offers 15 beds/5 baths in over 6,300 square feet (per tax records).  Two units are currently tenant occupied, one is vacant and two are owner occupied.  This property was last sold in 1987 and simply oozes classic, early Edwardian details and craftsmanship.   There are four (4) parking spaces at the rear of the property accessible by Ames Alley.  Ideally located at the border of Noe Valley and the city's vibrant Mission District.  Shopping, public transportation, restaurants and even a coin-op laundromat are mere steps away."
